## 7. Database and safety record

Additive schema code introduced:

| Store | Addition | Preservation behavior |
|---|---|---|
| Decision journal | `candidate_decision_history` and index | Appends evaluation/Supervisor events atomically with latest state; no historical backfill |
| Position evidence | `position_deal_evidence` and index | Immutable account/deal-keyed records; idempotence and conflict rollback |
| Position evidence | `position_deal_account_binding` | Exact historical Demo login/server/mode binding; rejects legacy adoption or identity change |

The worker lazily initializes `runtime/position_deal_evidence.sqlite3` on an eligible
idle collection pass. Schema behavior has been tested on disposable databases;
no deployed runtime database was migrated here. Verified backups and recovery
procedures are required before running the upgraded code on existing runtime data.

Rechecked scoped preservation: **47 of 50 existing Python files** across agents,
coordination, risk, strategy, Supervisor, execution and security match the RC16
baseline. The three intentional differences are `demo_transport.py`,
`reconciliation.py`, and `trade_management.py` under `atlas/execution`.

The account-worker entrypoint and diagnostic/manager/server files are also changed
outside that 50-file comparison. Therefore **do not claim all runtime files are
unchanged**. Fundamental Strategy #1, Supervisor/risk authority, MFA/RBAC and Live
prohibition were not redesigned. Baseline RC16 was not edited; no credentials,
Owner account or actual Demo permission were reset to make tests pass.

